{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Export every event an app tracks as JSON Schema that people and services outside the app can read, and check each change against the plan committed before it."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","title":"TrackingPlans","externalID":"TrackingPlans","modules":[{"name":"TrackingPlans"}]},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/File","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanError"],"title":"Making a plan","anchor":"Making-a-plan"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/files","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/files(carryingForward:)","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/write(to:)","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanCommand"],"title":"Writing a plan","anchor":"Writing-a-plan"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/igluFiles(vendor:registry:carryingForward:)","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/writeIgluRegistry(to:vendor:registry:)","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/IgluRegistry","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/IgluExportError"],"title":"Exporting an Iglu registry","anchor":"Exporting-an-Iglu-registry"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/check(against:)","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/check(againstDirectory:)","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanCheck","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanDifference"],"title":"Checking a plan","anchor":"Checking-a-plan"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A tracking plan is the contract between an app and whoever reads its events: dashboards, a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"warehouse, a collector, another platform’s client. Each event’s document gives its version,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"consent category, properties and their JSON types, which ones every payload holds, and which are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":", in a form that needs no Swift to read. Committed beside the events, it puts every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"change to them in the pull request as a JSON diff. Its check says which changes break what has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"already shipped: payloads from installed app versions that a validating collector would reject,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and stored records the app could no longer decode."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" turns events’ schemas into files: an index, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tracking-plan.json"},{"type":"text","text":", and for each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event a JSON Schema (draft 2020-12) document and an example payload. The files are values, so the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same schemas give the same bytes on every run and platform, ready to commit for the people and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tools outside the app."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Checking compares the plan the events make now with the committed one by what the files mean. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanCheck","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is a match, a plan that is only out of date, or one with a breaking"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"difference: a change that, at the same version, would leave a stored record or an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"already-released app’s payload unable to decode or validate. Each "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanDifference","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" names"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the event, the property and the change, and says whether it is breaking."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Only code compiled against the app’s event types can read their schemas, so the app writes a small","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"executable of its own: a type that conforms to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanCommand","type":"reference"},{"text":", marked ","type":"text"},{"code":"@main","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". It writes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the plan to a directory, or checks it with ","type":"text"},{"code":"check","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". To run the check from the app’s tests instead,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"use ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlanTesting","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The schemas usually come from ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventMacros","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"):","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/init()","type":"reference"},{"text":" takes every ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the program and the library’s own events, found at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"run time, and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/init(schemas:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" takes a list.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The module is a product of its own that "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves out."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import TrackingPlans","import Traffluent","","@Event(name: \"signed_up\")","struct SignedUp {","    var plan: String","}","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()  \/\/ every @Event in the program, and the library's own","let check = plan.check(against: plan.files)  \/\/ .matches","let paths = plan.files.map(\\.path)","\/\/ [\"tracking-plan.json\", ..., \"signed_up.v1.schema.json\", \"signed_up.v1.example.json\"]"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plan also writes the schemas of an Iglu registry, which a Snowplow pipeline validates events"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"against ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/igluFiles(vendor:registry:carryingForward:)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/writeIgluRegistry(to:vendor:registry:)"},{"type":"text","text":"). Version N of an event is SchemaVer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"N-0-0"},{"type":"text","text":". For Iglu Server, a compatible change at the same version is the next addition, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"N-0-1"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and on, superseding the earlier ones; a static repository doesn’t supersede, so there the export"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"refuses it, and so it does a breaking change for either kind: raise the event’s version."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingplanworkflow","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers the executable, the command plugins and the test."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/trackingplans"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"references":{"doc://TrackingPlans/documentation/TrackingPlans":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/trackingplans","abstract":[{"text":"Export every event an app tracks as JSON Schema that people and services outside the app can read, and check each change against the plan committed before it.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","title":"TrackingPlans","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans"},"doc://TrackingPlans/documentation/TrackingPlans/TrackingPlan/check(against:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/check(against:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"check"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"against"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"TrackingPlan","preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"File","preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV4FileV"},{"kind":"text","text":"]) -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"TrackingPlanCheck","preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A9PlanCheckO"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Compares the plan with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"committed"},{"type":"text","text":", the files of a plan exported before, and reports every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"difference."}],"url":"\/documentation\/trackingplans\/trackingplan\/check(against:)","type":"topic","title":"check(against:)"},"doc://TrackingPlans/documentation/TrackingPlans/TrackingPlanError":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why schemas can’t make a tracking plan."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TrackingPlanError"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TrackingPlanError"}],"title":"TrackingPlanError","url":"\/documentation\/trackingplans\/trackingplanerror","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanError"},"doc://TrackingPlans/documentation/TrackingPlans/TrackingPlan/init()":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The plan of every event the program declares with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":", and of the library’s own, or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an error naming the first rule they break."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"() "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A9PlanErrorO","text":"TrackingPlanError"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"title":"init()","url":"\/documentation\/trackingplans\/trackingplan\/init()","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/init()"},"doc://TrackingPlans/documentation/TrackingPlans/TrackingPlan/schemas":{"title":"schemas","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/schemas","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/trackingplans\/trackingplan\/schemas","abstract":[{"tex